<Base title="Federica Iengo | AI Search, GEO/AEO/SEO & Data Engineering" description="Independent AI Search, GEO, AEO and SEO research alongside practical data engineering, SQL, Python, Snowflake and dbt projects.">
<section class="hero">
<p class="eyebrow">AI Search · GEO · AEO · SEO | Data Engineering</p>
<h1>I make complex information easier to understand, measure and use.</h1>
<p class="lead">I work across AI Search, GEO, AEO and SEO research and practical data engineering. I study how search systems retrieve and cite information, and use SQL, Python, Snowflake and dbt to build, test and reconcile reliable datasets.</p><p class="scope-note">Independent portfolio projects · Methods, evidence and limitations documented · Open to remote opportunities from Italy.</p>
<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/projects/">Explore projects</a><a class="button" href="/research/">Research methods</a><a class="about-link" href="/about/">About me <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
</section>

<section class="proof">
<p class="eyebrow">Current focus</p>
<div class="grid">
<article class="card"><h3>Measure</h3><p>Build reproducible datasets and metrics for AI visibility, citations, retrieval and competitive analysis.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Diagnose</h3><p>Find content, entity, evidence and data-quality gaps instead of reducing a problem to a single score.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Improve</h3><p>Turn findings into testable changes, then keep proposed interventions separate from measured outcomes.</p></article>
</div>
</section>

<section>
<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p><h2>Projects built around evidence</h2></div><a href="/projects/">View all projects →</a></div>
<div class="grid featured">
<a class="card project-card" href="/projects/seo-aeo-geo-optimization/"><span class="project-type">AI Search · Independent case study</span><h3>SEO/AEO/GEO Optimization</h3><p>An independent Notion case study moving from public baseline and query fan-out to diagnosis, proposed optimization and controlled measurement design.</p><span class="project-link">Read case study →</span></a>
<a class="card project-card" href="/projects/ai-search-competitive-intelligence/"><span class="project-type">AI Search · Benchmark protocol</span><h3>AI Search Competitive Intelligence</h3><p>A controlled benchmark across Notion, Asana, ClickUp and monday.com using 35 frozen prompts, first-party evidence and auditable scoring rules. AI response observations are pending.</p><span class="project-link">Explore benchmark →</span></a>
<article class="card project-card"><span class="project-type">Data · Snowflake · dbt · Power BI</span><h3>E-Commerce Revenue & Operations Analytics</h3><p>End-to-end analytics pipeline: 28 dbt models, 249 passing tests and a four-page Power BI report. Includes order lifecycle and financial reconciliation analysis.</p><a class="source-link" href="/projects/ecommerce-technical-evidence/">Read the financial reconciliation case study →</a><br><a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/federicaiengo/data-analytics-portfolio/tree/main/projects/ecommerce-revenue-operations-analytics" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect code & report ↗</a></article>
<article class="card project-card"><span class="project-type">Data · PostgreSQL · Tableau</span><h3>Insurance Claims Analytics</h3><p>SQL analysis of 10,000 insurance claims, exposure concentration and data quality, with an executive Tableau dashboard.</p><a class="source-link" href="/projects/insurance-claims-evidence/">Read the insurance claims case study →</a><br><a class="source-link" href="https://github.com/federicaiengo/data-analytics-portfolio/tree/main/projects/insurance-claims-analytics" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect project & dashboard ↗</a></article>
</div>
</section>

<section class="principle">
<p class="eyebrow">Working principle</p>
<h2>Evidence first. Claims second.</h2>
<p>I keep observed facts, analysis, proposed changes and measured outcomes separate. That matters in data work, and it matters just as much when evaluating visibility in AI-generated answers.</p>
</section>
</Base>

